imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail 2x"},"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/d2/US278ACRSSI.svg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:US278ACRSSI.svg","descriptionshorturl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?curid=36159390","sha1":"3c9fa0b5900bf0c52e21da8cac4fe4ea1cc61363","extmetadata":{"DateTime":{"value":"2014-10-15 14:18:02","source":"mediawiki-metadata","hidden":""},"ObjectName":{"value":"US278ACRSSI","source":"mediawiki-metadata"},"CommonsMetadataExtension":{"value":1.2,"source":"extension","hidden":""},"Categories":{"value":"GFDL|License migration redundant|278th Armored Cavalry Regiment (United States)|CC-BY-SA-4.0,3.0,2.5,2.0,1.0|Self-published work|PD US Army USAIOH|Valid SVG created with Adobe Illustrator|Images created by Fred the Oyster|US Army Regimental Shoulder Sleeve Insignia|Stars in military insignia","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"Assessments":{"value":"","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"ImageDescription":{"value":"*On a disc 2⅝ inches (6.67cm) in diameter a white-edged blue triskelion with lower leg vertical between three white five-pointed stars on a green background all inclosed by a ⅛ inch (0.32cm) white border.\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"Symbolism\">Symbolism</h3></div>\n<ul><li>The green background with three stars refers to the hickory tree crest of the Tennessee ARNG.</li>\n<li>The wavy blue three-armed partition represents the coming together of the Holston and the French Broad Rivers to form the beginning of the Tennessee River in Knoxville, where the regiment's headquarters is located.</li></ul>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"Background\">Background</h3></div>\n<ul><li>The shoulder sleeve insignia was originally approved for the 278th Infantry Brigade on 19 March 1974.</li>\n<li>It was redesignated for the 278th Armored Cavalry Regiment on 19 August 1977.</li></ul>\n- US Army Institute of Heraldry","source":"commons-desc-page"},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"2014-10-15","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Credit":{"value":"<span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:US278ACRSSI.PNG\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/US278ACRSSI.PNG/120px-US278ACRSSI.PNG?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"100\" height=\"99\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/65/US278ACRSSI.PNG?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x\" data-file-width=\"167\" data-file-height=\"165\"></a></span>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Artist":{"value":"<a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/User:Fred_the_Oyster\" title=\"User:Fred the Oyster\">Fred the Oyster</a><br><div lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\" class=\"plainlinks\">\n<table cellspacing=\"0\" style=\"color:inherit;background:var(--background-color-success-subtle,#EFE);border:1px solid #55B05A;margin:.1em;width:;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"height:29px;line-height:2.1em;padding:0;vertical-align:middle\"><span class=\"mw-valign-top\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://validator.w3.org/\" rel=\"nofollow\"><img alt=\"W3C\" src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/Valid_SVG_1.1_%28green%29.svg/120px-Valid_SVG_1.1_%28green%29.svg.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"88\" height=\"30\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/Valid_SVG_1.1_%28green%29.svg/250px-Valid_SVG_1.1_%28green%29.svg.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"91\" data-file-height=\"31\"></a></span><span style=\"visibility:hidden; color:transparent;\">i</span>The source code of this  <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Help:SVG\" title=\"Help:SVG\">SVG</a> is <span class=\"plainlinks\" style=\"background:#CFA; color: inherit;\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://validator.w3.org/check?uri=https%3A%2F%2Fcommons.wikimedia.org%2Fwiki%2FSpecial%3AFilepath%2FUS278ACRSSI.svg&amp;doctype=Inline\">valid</a></span>.\n</td></tr></tbody></table> </div><div style=\"display:table;width:;vertical-align:middle;direction:ltr;float:left;line-height:22px;height:24px;font-size:.96em;margin:0px;padding:2px 4px 2px 6px;color:var(--color-base,#000);background:var(--background-color-neutral-subtle,#F8F9FA);border:1px solid #BAB;border-collapse:separate;border-spacing:0px;;\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Adobe-yes.svg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Adobe-yes.svg/40px-Adobe-yes.svg.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"23\" height=\"22\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Adobe-yes.svg/60px-Adobe-yes.svg.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"342\" data-file-height=\"322\"></a></span> This  <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vector_images\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:Vector images\">vector image</a> was created with <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adobe_Illustrator\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:Adobe Illustrator\">Adobe Illustrator</a> by v.</div>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Permission":{"value":"<i>This image shows a <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/flag\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:flag\">flag</a>, a <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/coat_of_arms\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:coat of arms\">coat of arms</a>, a <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/seal_(device)\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:seal (device)\">seal</a> or some other official <b><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/insignia\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:insignia\">insignia</a></b> produced by the <b><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States_Army_Institute_of_Heraldry\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:United States Army Institute of Heraldry\">United States Army Institute of Heraldry</a></b>.  It is in the <b><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/public_domain\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:public domain\">public domain</a></b> but its use is restricted by <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.gpo.gov/fdsys/pkg/USCODE-2010-title18/pdf/USCODE-2010-title18-partI-chap33-sec704.pdf\">Title 18, United States Code, Section 704</a> <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external autonumber\" href=\"https://www.law.cornell.edu/uscode/text/18/704\">[1]</a> and the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.gpo.gov/fdsys/granule/CFR-2012-title32-vol3/CFR-2012-title32-vol3-part507/content-detail.html\">Code of Federal Regulations (32 CFR, Part 507)</a> <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external autonumber\" href=\"https://www.ecfr.gov/cgi-bin/text-idx?mc=true&amp;node=pt32.3.507&amp;rgn=div5\">[2]</a>, <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external autonumber\" href=\"https://www.law.cornell.edu/cfr/text/32/part-507\">[3]</a>.  Permission to use these images in the USA for most commercial purposes must be obtained from The Institute of Heraldry prior to their use.</i>","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"Public domain","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"UsageTerms":{"value":"Public domain","source":"commons-desc-page"},"AttributionRequired":{"value":"false","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"Copyrighted":{"value":"False","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"Restrictions":{"value":"","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"License":{"value":"pd","source":"commons-templates","hidden":""}},"mime":"image/svg+xml"}],"revisions":[{"revid":1237509117,"parentid":1017854293,"timestamp":"2026-06-24T10:54:05Z","slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","content":"== {{int:filedesc}} ==\n{{Information\n|Description    ={{en|1=\n*On a disc 2⅝ inches (6.67cm) in diameter a white-edged blue triskelion with lower leg vertical between three white five-pointed stars on a green background all inclosed by a ⅛ inch (0.32cm) white border.\n\n===Symbolism===\n\n*The green background with three stars refers to the hickory tree crest of the Tennessee ARNG.\n*The wavy blue three-armed partition represents the coming together of the Holston and the French Broad Rivers to form the beginning of the Tennessee River in Knoxville, where the regiment's headquarters is located.\n\n===Background===\n\n*The shoulder sleeve insignia was originally approved for the 278th Infantry Brigade on 19 March 1974.\n*It was redesignated for the 278th Armored Cavalry Regiment on 19 August 1977.\n\n- US Army Institute of Heraldry}}\n|Source         =[[File:US278ACRSSI.PNG|100px]]\n|Author         =[[User:Fred the Oyster|Fred the Oyster]]<br/>{{Adobe|v}}\n|Date           =2014-10-15\n|Permission     ={{PD-USGov-Military-Army-USAIOH}}\n|other_versions =\n}}\n\n== {{int:license-header}} ==\n{{self|GFDL|cc-by-sa-all|migration=redundant}}\n\n[[Category:US Army Regimental Shoulder Sleeve Insignia]]\n[[Category:Stars in military insignia]]\n[[Category:Images created by Fred the Oyster]]\n[[Category:278th Armored Cavalry Regiment (United States)]]"}}}]},{"pageid":48228834,"ns":6,"title":"File:Governors Twelve Tab-ABU.png","imagerepository":"local","imageinfo":[{"timestamp":"2016-11-12T15:19:24Z","user":"McChizzle","size":50817,"width":306,"height":107,"thumburl":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/bb/Governors_Twelve_Tab-ABU.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","thumbwidth":480,"thum