=\"extiw\" title=\"en:United States Army\">United States Army</a> Marksmanship Unit (USAMU), Public Affairs","source":"commons-desc-page"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"Public domain","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"UsageTerms":{"value":"Public domain","source":"commons-desc-page"},"AttributionRequired":{"value":"false","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"Copyrighted":{"value":"False","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"Restrictions":{"value":"","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"License":{"value":"pd","source":"commons-templates","hidden":""}},"mime":"image/png"}],"revisions":[{"revid":1275935441,"parentid":912516755,"timestamp":"2026-09-13T13:41:39Z","slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","content":"== {{int:filedesc}} ==\n{{Information\n|Description={{en|Image of the [[:en:Army Combat Uniform|Army Combat Uniform]] (ACU) version of the [[:en:Missouri National Guard|Missouri National Guard]] Governor's Twelve Tab}}\n|Source=Extracted and enhanced from https://www.flickr.com/photos/missouriguard/6987578737/in/photostream/\n|Date=2012-03-10\n|Author=Mike Molinaro, [[:en:United States Army|United States Army]] Marksmanship Unit (USAMU), Public Affairs\n|Permission=\n|other_versions=[[:en:File:Mog12r.jpg|100px]] Missouri National Guard's General's Twelve Ribbon\n}}\n\n== {{int:license-header}} ==\n{{PD-USGov-Military-Army}}\n{{PD-USGov-Military-Award}}\n{{PD-USGov-Military-Badge}}\n\n== {{Original upload log}} ==\n{{original description|en.wikipedia|Governors+Twelve+Tab-ABU.png}}\n{| class=\"wikitable\"\n! {{int:filehist-datetime}} !! {{int:filehist-dimensions}} !! {{int:filehist-user}} !! {{int:filehist-comment}}\n|-\n| 2015-02-09 14:42 || 306×107× (131524 bytes) || [[:en:User:McChizzle|McChizzle]] || ''<nowiki>{{Information |Description= Image of the [[Army Combat Uniform]] (ACU) version of the [[Missouri National Guard]] Governor's Twelve Tab |Source= Extracted and enhanced from https://www.flickr.com/photos/missouriguard/6987578737/in/photostream/ |Date= 1...</nowiki>''\n|}\n\n\n[[Category:United States Army]]\n[[Category:US Army Shoulder Tabs (individual tabs)]]"}}}]},{"pageid":115888340,"ns":6,"title":"File:SETAF.png","imagerepository":"local","imageinfo":[{"timestamp":"2022-03-07T23:14:40Z","user":"Kwasura","size":29398,"width":200,"height":304,"thumburl":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/d6/SETAF.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","thumbwidth":316,"thumbheight":480,"thumbattribs":{"src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/d6/SETAF.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","decoding":"async","loading":"lazy","width":316,"height":480},"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/d6/SETAF.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:SETAF.png","descriptionshorturl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?curid=115888340","sha1":"eedc4f772556a7ad509298fd22b8c2d8967a57ae","extmetadata":{"DateTime":{"value":"2022-03-07 23:14:40","source":"mediawiki-metadata","hidden":""},"ObjectName":{"value":"SETAF","source":"mediawiki-metadata"},"CommonsMetadataExtension":{"value":1.2,"source":"extension","hidden":""},"Categories":{"value":"Shoulder Sleeve Insignia of the United States Army (SSI)|PD US Army USAIOH","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"Assessments":{"value":"","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"ImageDescription":{"value":"The shoulder sleeve insignia was originally approved for the Southern European Task Force on 6 December 1955.  On 2 April 1958, it was redesignated for the United States Army Southern European Task Force.  The description and symbolism was amended to delete reference to the tab \"SETAF\" on 9 February 1962.  The insignia was amended to change the description on 6 December 1998. On 27 February 2001, the shoulder sleeve insignia was amended to include an airborne tab.  The insignia was amended to delete the airborne tab and add the \"\"SETAF\" tab on 4 September 2008.","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Credit":{"value":"<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://tioh.army.mil/\">https://tioh.army.mil/</a>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Artist":{"value":"US Army","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Permission":{"value":"<i>This image shows a <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/flag\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:flag\">flag</a>, a <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/coat_of_arms\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:coat of arms\">coat of arms</a>, a <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/seal_(device)\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:seal (device)\">seal</a> or some other official <b><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/insignia\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:insignia\">insignia</a></b> produced by the <b><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States_Army_Institute_of_Heraldry\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:United States Army Institute of Heraldry\">United States Army Institute of Heraldry</a></b>.  It is in the <b><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/public_domain\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:public domain\">public domain</a></b> but its use is restricted by <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.gpo.gov/fdsys/pkg/USCODE-2010-title18/pdf/USCODE-2010-title18-partI-chap33-sec704.pdf\">Title 18, United States Code, Section 704</a> <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external autonumber\" href=\"https://www.law.cornell.edu/uscode/text/18/704\">[1]</a> and the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.gpo.gov/fdsys/granule/CFR-2012-title32-vol3/CFR-2012-title32-vol3-part507/content-detail.html\">Code of Federal Regulations (32 CFR, Part 507)</a> <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external autonumber\" href=\"https://www.ecfr.gov/cgi-bin/text-idx?mc=true&amp;node=pt32.3.507&amp;rgn=div5\">[2]</a>, <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external autonumber\" href=\"https://www.law.cornell.edu/cfr/text/32/part-507\">[3]</a>.  Permission to use these images in the USA for most commercial purposes must be obtained from The Institute of Heraldry prior to their use.</i>","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"Public domain","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"UsageTerms":{"value":"Public domain","source":"commons-desc-page"},"AttributionRequired":{"value":"false","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"Copyrighted":{"value":"False","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"Restrictions":{"value":"","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"License":{"value":"pd","source":"commons-templates","hidden":""}},"mime":"image/png"}],"revisions":[{"revid":912895905,"parentid":678188835,"timestamp":"2024-08-20T08:15:38Z","slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","content":"== {{int:filedesc}} ==\n{{Information\n|Description=The shoulder sleeve insignia was originally approved for the Southern European Task Force on 6 December 1955.  On 2 April 1958, it was redesignated for the United States Army Southern European Task Force.  The description and symbolism was amended to delete reference to the tab \"SETAF\" on 9 February 1962.  The insignia was amended to change the description on 6 December 1998. On 27 February 2001, the shoulder sleeve insignia was amended to include an airborne tab.  The insignia was amended to delete the airborne tab and add the \"\"SETAF\" tab on 4 September 2008. \n|Source=https://tioh.army.mil/\n|Date=\n|Author=US Army\n|Permission= {{PD-USGov-Military-Army-USAIOH}}\n|other_versions=\n}}\n\n[[Category:Shoulder Sleeve Insignia of the United States Army (SSI)]]"}}}]},{"pageid":125547931,"ns":6,"title":"File:3rd Infantry Division Artillery Crest.png","imagerepository":"local","imageinfo":[{"timestamp":"2022-11-16T03:37:16Z","user":"Coldstreamer20","size":130426,"width":241,"height":162,"thumburl":"https://